---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../../config/site";
---

<Layout title="About" description="About the database, its data sources, and attribution." canonicalPath="/about">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold">About &amp; attribution</h1>

    <div class="prose-invert mt-6 space-y-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-text">
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-muted">About {siteConfig.name}</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-muted">
          {siteConfig.name} tracks publicly disclosed software vulnerabilities and makes them searchable for security teams,
          researchers, system administrators, and developers across Bangladesh. Each entry is normalized into a consistent format
          covering severity, affected products, technical detail, and remediation references, so vulnerabilities can be found and
          assessed quickly regardless of which organization originally disclosed them.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-muted">Data sources</h2>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-inside list-disc space-y-2 text-muted">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-text">CVE Program (cve.org)</strong> — the primary source for vulnerability records, updated on a
            regular schedule.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-text">CISA Known Exploited Vulnerabilities (KEV)</strong> — optional enrichment. When a CVE appears
            in CISA's KEV catalog, that fact is attributed to CISA explicitly and never inferred.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3 text-muted">
          Every field in every record keeps track of which source it came from (see the "Data sources" panel on each vulnerability's
          page). Source data is never merged or blended without preserving that attribution.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-muted">What we don't do</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-muted">
          We don't infer exploitation status, invent severity scores or weakness classifications that a source didn't provide, or
          fabricate any field. Where information isn't available from a source, it's shown as unavailable — never guessed.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-muted">Attribution &amp; disclaimer</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-muted">
          Vulnerability record data is sourced from and redistributed under the terms published by the CVE Program (CVE Record data
          is made available under CC0 1.0 by MITRE / the CVE Program); consult
          <a href="https://www.cve.org/Legal/TermsOfUse" class="text-accent hover:underline" rel="noopener noreferrer">cve.org's terms of use</a>
          for the authoritative statement. {siteConfig.name} is an independent project and is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or
          officially connected to MITRE, the CVE Program, NVD, or CISA.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-muted">Contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-muted">
          Found an error in how a record is displayed, or something missing? Use the "Report an issue" link in the footer to let us
          know.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
